\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Father, in high heaven dwelling,
\par May our evening song be telling
\par Of Thy mercy large and free:
\par Through the day Thy love hath fed us,
\par Through the day Thy care hath led us,
\par With divinest charity.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. This day's sins, O pardon, Saviour!
\par Evil thoughts, perverse behaviour,
\par Envy, pride, and vanity;
\par From the world, the flesh, deliver,
\par Save us now, and save us ever,
\par O Thou Lamb of Calvary!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. From enticements of the devil,
\par From the might of spirits evil,
\par Be our shield and panoply;
\par Let Thy power this night defend us,
\par And a heavenly peace attend us,
\par And angelic company.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Whilst the night- dews are distilling,
\par Holy Ghost, each heart be filling,
\par With Thine own serenity;
\par Softly let our eyes be closing,
\par While on Thee the soul reposing,
\par Ever- blessed Trinity.
\par                         Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

